            },
    "parts":  [
                  "Look at the shape behind God, in Michelangelo's Creation of Adam.",
                  "In nineteen ninety, a medical journal printed the idea that it is a human brain.",
                  "The author, Meshberger, read it as God giving Adam intelligence, not only life.",
                  "In twenty ten, two Johns Hopkins authors, Suk and Tamargo, went further.",
                  "They saw a brain stem in God's neck, in another panel of the same ceiling.",
                  "Could a painter know what a brain looks like?",
                  "His biographer, Condivi, wrote that Michelangelo did so many dissections that he outdid the professionals.",
                  "But doctors saw something else in that same neck.",
                  "Two doctors saw a goiter there instead.",
                  "Skeptics ask: are we just seeing the man in the moon?",
                  "Our reading: the brain is a modern idea about the painting. It is not a documented fact.",
                  "Subscribe for the next one: why cold can feel wet."
              ],
